//RS /// The type a built-in method dispatches on, once compile-time-only tag
//RS /// wrappers are erased. Shared by `tir_recv_jet_ty` and by `builtin_recv_ty`
//RS /// (TIR/lower/builtins.rs), which closes this function's struct-`Field` hole for
//RS /// the builtin table — one tag rule, read the same way from both.
//RS ///
//RS /// D-TAINT1/D-TAG-SURFACE1: most `Type::Tagged` markers (the terminal
//RS /// capability report's own D-PROCESS-SESSION2 tag, `#Input`/other user
//RS /// taint facts, …) are compile-time-only dataflow facts with no runtime
//RS /// representation — the same erasure `Expr::Tainted` gets in
//RS /// `expr_in_subset` (TIR/subset/expressions.rs). Builtin-method
//RS /// dispatch must see the real underlying type (String/List/Map/…)
//RS /// or a tagged receiver's `.split()`/`.get()`/etc. misses the curated
//RS /// `TBuiltinOp` fast path and falls back to a generic call the JIT
//RS /// declines to native-compile.
//RS ///
//RS /// The compiler-owned exceptions mirror sema's OWN rule at
//RS /// `infer_method_call` (Sema/CheckerInfer/calls/method_calls.rs,
//RS /// "Most fact tags are type-transparent"): SharedGuard read/edit and
//RS /// the crypto nominal tag carry method POLICY, not just a dataflow
//RS /// fact — `SharedGuard.wait()` dispatches through the tagged type's
//RS /// own handle-method table, not a generic `TypeName::method` lookup.
